// probe_settle.hml — acceptance probe for src/sim/settle.hml (and worldgen's
// multi-site block).  Run it FROM THE NIGHTSHADE REPO ROOT, both ways:
//
//     hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_settle.hml -o /tmp/psettle && /tmp/psettle
//     hemlock  tools/probe_settle.hml
//
// It exits 1 on any failure AND on an assertion-count mismatch — a probe that
// silently stops running half its checks is worse than no probe.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS PROBE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT ONLY REPORTS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSERTED: the DESIGN.  Every relationship SETTLEMENT.md and DIRECTION.md
// state — the ladder is monotone, growth only appends, a plot once assigned
// keeps its building, invalid plots are skipped and never moved, the field is
// capped, entropy falls with light, the Foundry's four gates are all necessary,
// nothing disarms the player, the save round-trips bit-identically, and two
// settlements are never closer than 1000 m.
//
// ASSERTED WITH A LITERAL: the design ANCHORS — 10/32/72 grid points,
// 512/1024/2048 CORE_LUX, T1/T2/T4, CL_MAX 4096, 72 plots, 16 m green, 1000 m
// separation, the 0/2/9/15 decay ladder, the 60/120/200/300/420 ammo ladder.
// CLAUDE.md rule 5: enemy caps were once mutable with every probe green because
// the assertions were relative to the config value.
//
// ONLY REPORTED, deliberately: section N, the plot-validity survey.  It prints a
// measurement that FAILS SETTLEMENT.md §5.4's claim that "the lattice never runs
// out", with the numbers, and it does NOT exit 1 — because the number it is
// measuring is a property of `sm_building`'s footing course, which this task
// does not own, and CLAUDE.md §1.2 is explicit that a probe which false-fails on
// somebody else's decision trains everyone to ignore red.  The finding is in the
// task report where a human will read it.

